// `struct:` names a struct by its typedef or its tag: a union is an opaque value, a pointer a handle,
// and a scalar no struct; the name is a string, and a data type mirrors one thing.
// error: `struct:` names the C struct the type mirrors, and `union as_some` is a union, whose fields share their memory, so it crosses as an opaque value, a class declared `@c(value: "union as_some")`
// error: `struct:` names the C struct the type mirrors, and `as_point *` is a pointer: a struct C allocates is a handle, and a mirror names the struct itself
// error: `struct:` names the C struct the type mirrors, and `unsigned` is not a struct
// error: `struct:` takes a string, as in `struct: "cairo_matrix_t"`
// error: `@c` on a data type mirrors a C struct with `struct:`, as in `@c(struct: "cairo_matrix_t")`

@c(struct: "union as_some")
data Union(i: int)

@c(struct: "as_point *")
data Pointer(x: real)

@c(struct: "unsigned")
data Scalar(x: int)

@c(struct: as_point)
data Bare(x: real)

@c(struct: "as_point", "as_point")
data Positional(x: real)

main() = 0
